-- Fixture for "l4 batch: when a declared breach was observed".
--
-- Alice misses 5 and the one event, at 20, reveals it. The declared breach
-- her LEST reaches takes effect at 5 and is observed at 20, the revealing
-- event, both bare and as an operand of a RAND (NOTE [A declared breach in
-- a RAND is observed at the revealing event] in L4.EvaluateLazy.Machine).

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Alice, Bob
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF deliver, noop

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`bare` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST deliver WITHIN 5 LEST BREACH BY Alice

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`in a RAND` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST deliver WITHIN 5 LEST (FULFILLED RAND (BREACH BY Alice))

#TRACE `bare` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Alice DOES noop AT 20

#TRACE `in a RAND` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Alice DOES noop AT 20

@export default trivial entrypoint so batch has a function to call
alwaysTrue MEANS TRUE
